INT. CORPORATE BALL PIT, SYNERGY FLOOR - DAY

A glass-walled "ideation lounge" holding forty thousand primary-coloured plastic balls. A motivational neon sign reads FAIL FORWARD.

DEBORAH PLUMMER, forties, VP of People, stands on a bench with a clicker, announcing the fun. KHALID RASHAD, thirty, sits waist-deep in the balls with a laptop balanced on his knees, typing, while BRAD WEXLER, intern, wades past with a tray of lukewarm kombucha, drops two cups, apologises, drops a third, and sinks quietly out of sight.

DEBORAH
Okay, team! Quarterly Wins!

KHALID
Deb, I have a deadline.

DEBORAH
This is the deadline.

KHALID
This is a pit.

Brad's head resurfaces. A red ball sits on it like a hat.

BRAD
I think I've lost a shoe.
